## Webhook URLs containing credentials

With Terraform 1.11.1 or later, use `webhook.url_wo` and `webhook.url_wo_version` to keep a webhook destination URL out of plans and state. Supply the URL from an ephemeral variable or ephemeral resource; an ordinary data source still stores its result in state.

```hcl
variable "webhook_url" {
  type      = string
  sensitive = true
  ephemeral = true
}

resource "buildkite_notification_service" "webhook" {
  provider_type = "webhook"

  webhook = {
    url_wo         = var.webhook_url
    url_wo_version = 1
    events         = ["build.finished"]
  }
}
```

Increment `url_wo_version` whenever the URL changes. The provider sends the URL on creation and when this version changes. Changing only the ephemeral value, or updating unrelated settings, does not update the destination. Terraform cannot detect URL changes made outside Terraform when using `url_wo`.

To migrate an existing resource, replace `url` with `url_wo`, add `url_wo_version`, and apply. This removes `url` from the current resource state without replacing the notification service. Previous state versions and saved plans can still contain the old URL; rotate credentials that have already been stored and handle historical artifacts according to your state backend's retention controls.

`url` remains available for existing configurations and Terraform versions before 1.11.1. The write-only argument covers only the destination URL; other secret attributes such as `webhook.token` retain their existing state behavior.

